; vivarium.decision-log.udon — scenario-corpus edition
; Pseudo-real: same genre as arch/vivarium/DECISIONS.decision-log.udon.
; FAST-APPEND, INTERLEAVE-FREE — the property the multi-agent scenarios
; exercise: each |decision is a SELF-CONTAINED, TOP-LEVEL block (column 0).
; There is NO wrapping parent element, so a new entry appends at EOF with no
; need to read, parse, or re-close anything above it. Append the whole block
; in ONE write, preceded by a single blank line (O_APPEND makes a single
; write atomic on POSIX, so concurrent agents cannot interleave entries).
; Slugs are unique and kebab-case; duplicate-slug detection is the
; Document-layer duplicate-definition policy, checked after assembly, never
; during the streaming parse.
;
; ENTRY SHAPE: header line carries slug + fixed fields inline
;   (|decision[slug] :date <d> :by <auth> :status <s> :topic <t>);
; metadata lines indented one field per line (:session always; :supersedes
; when used goes ON THE HEADER LINE so grep '^|decision\[' shows the chain);
; the STATEMENT is the entry's plain body text on one logical line;
; |reason and |impact carry the trail.
;
; AUTHORITY: joseph (his call; agent abstained) · us (joint — Joseph decided
; AND the agent sustains it) · claude (an agent's tactical call, logged so
; it does not fall through the cracks). Do not inflate.

|decision[fixture-groups-are-versioned] :date <2026-07-14> :by us :status decided :topic compliance
  :session 01Kx2mQpVv8sT4Ra
  Compliance is measured by version-scoped fixture groups; an implementation is compliant with core-vX iff it passes that group.
  |reason Tracked-in-prose compliance claims drift; a frozen group is checkable by anyone, forever.
  |impact fixtures/v0.8 frozen at the tag; v0.9 is the active burn-down group.
  |ref core/fixtures/README.md

|decision[scenario-corpus-is-pseudo-real] :date <2026-07-16> :by claude :status proposed :topic testing
  :session 01Mc9uTz5Wa9cWYb
  The BDD scenario corpus mirrors real consumer genres (process-map, lexicon, ordinum, operata) with its own content, so scenarios can mutate files freely without touching live documents.
  |reason Real consumer files are read-only from this repo's side; scenarios need to write.
  |impact test/scenarios/corpus/ carries the pseudo-real editions; CONSUMERS.md still governs the real ones.

|decision[paths-quoted-in-value-position] :date <2026-07-16> :by claude :status proposed :topic paths
  :session 01Mc9uTz5Wa9cWYb
  A path expression stored in an attribute value is always a QUOTED string; a bare leading | or @ in value position would parse as a node or reference value, not text.
  |reason The path language reuses UDON's own sigils, so bare paths collide with the value grammar at their first character; quoting is the only 0.9-legal carrier (a <path:...> envelope becomes the principled home once dialects land).
  |impact Every :path value in test/scenarios/features/ is quoted; the linter should eventually flag bare-sigil path-shaped values.

|decision[claim-requires-nil] :date <2026-07-18> :by us :status decided :topic operata
  :session 01Hf7dNq2Lp0Xw3E
  An intent claim is valid only if :claimed-by is nil at write time; a second claimant must fail loudly, never overwrite.
  |reason Two agents claiming one intent is the canonical lost-update; the guard belongs in the write path, not in etiquette.
  |impact operata.domain.udon carries :require-nil [claimed-by] on |update[claim]; the edit tool needs a compare-and-set precondition to honor it.
  |ref corpus/operata.domain.udon
